<title>POLAND: BOMB SCARE GROUNDS SWISSAIR AIRLINER IN VIENNA.</title>
<headline>BOMB SCARE GROUNDS SWISSAIR AIRLINER IN VIENNA.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-05-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>A Swissair passenger plane travelling from Krakow to Zurich made an emergency landing in Vienna on Sunday after an anonymous caller claimed there was a bomb on board, Polish police said.</p>
<p>The plane resumed its flight to Zurich after a thorough search by an Austrian bomb squad failed to turn up any explosives, Krakow police duty officer Adam Hapek told Reuters by telephone.</p>
<p>An anonymous woman caller reported the bomb to Krakow airport 20 minutes after the plane had taken off, Hapek said.</p>
<p>The plane, with 46 people aboard, was flying over Czech territory when the call was received. After consulting with the control tower the pilot made an emergency landing in Vienna.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
